From e07871958e6128194daee5b9e5bfc2aa6064eac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:58:49 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] model: keep a row's cells in a vector sized to them

A row's cells were a B-tree map, whose every node has room for eleven
cells: 496 bytes for a row of one cell to eleven. Keep them in a vector
sorted by column instead: the row costs its cells. A row filled cell by
cell grows by half its length (2, 4, 6, 9, 13...), and readers give the
spare room back once a sheet is read (`CellStore::shrink_to_fit`,
`Workbook::shrink_to_fit`, called by the XLSX reader and on open).

Moving cells (shift_rows, shift_cols, shift_cols_in_rows) works on whole
rows and row ends instead of cell by cell, which a vector would make
quadratic. Every operation behaves as before: a differential test runs
random sets, removals, shifts, range takes and snapshots against the old
B-tree store and compares cells, counts, ranges, diffs and JSON, which is
unchanged.
